WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.740
- So it's nice to see you in person.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.251
- Nice to see you in person.

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:04.084
- [Kelly Clarkson] I know last time-

00:00:04.084 --> 00:00:05.040
- We had a Zoom.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.220
- Yeah. And you had all
that crazy stuff behind you.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.300
I love that part of Zoom.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.224
You got to see who people were. (chuckles)

00:00:11.224 --> 00:00:12.870
- You get to see in people's houses.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:13.703
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:00:13.703 --> 00:00:16.650
You had just given your
wife I believe a brain

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.890
or something like a toy brick.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.199
- [Rainn Wilson] Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:20.160
- [Kelly Clarkson] 'Cause that's normal.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.240
- [Rainn Wilson] Yeah. I
gave my wife a human brain

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.430
for her birthday.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:24.930
- Yeah. (chuckles)

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:25.830
- She loved it.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.663
It's one of those...

00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:27.797
No, is it anatomical brain?

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:28.630
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.463
- You can take it apart
and see how it works.

00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:31.170
- [Kelly Clarkson] I
actually think that's cool.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.160
- [Rainn Wilson] It's educational.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.150
- [Kelly Clarkson] I'm being funny. Oh!

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:33.983
- [Rainn Wilson] There
she is, Holiday Reinhorn.

00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:34.816
- [Kelly Clarkson] I want that hat.

00:00:34.816 --> 00:00:36.372
- [Rainn Wilson] Isn't she lovely folks?

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:37.221
- Where are you?

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:38.068
- Yes she is. (claps)

00:00:38.068 --> 00:00:38.901
(audience claps)

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:39.734
Oh yes!

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.376
- Wait, where are you?

00:00:41.376 --> 00:00:42.209
Do you remember?

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:43.770
- This is in Central Oregon.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.300
We have a cabin up in
the mountains of Oregon.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.657
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's beautiful.

00:00:46.657 --> 00:00:48.450
- [Rainn Wilson] Yeah,
don't go there. Okay.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.936
- [Kelly Clarkson] Don't
go there. (chuckles)

00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:50.940
Yeah. Like keep it nice and small.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.170
I have a place in Montana, I get it.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.580
Yeah. You like you like it small.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.380
So one thing we didn't
talk about last time,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.360
you play bassoon I didn't know that.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.910
- Yeah, you need a
bassoonist in your band.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.081
- [Kelly Clarkson] Totally.

00:01:01.081 --> 00:01:01.914
- Yeah?

00:01:01.914 --> 00:01:02.747
- Yeah.

00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:03.580
- What do you pay?

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:04.481
- Well, just free 95. (laughs)

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.730
(? laughs)

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.529
We play for our heart. (chuckles)

00:01:07.529 --> 00:01:09.300
No, no. We will pay you.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.200
Do you like playing bassoon?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.250
How long have you been playing bassoon?

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.100
- I started bassoon in like
the seventh or eighth grade.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.230
- I love how many times
we've said bassoon thus far.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.063
- [Rainn Wilson] Yes.

00:01:17.063 --> 00:01:19.007
I don't think a bassoon has been played

00:01:19.007 --> 00:01:21.630
as much, has been said as much. (chuckles)

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.920
- No one plays the bassoon!

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:23.850
Like how in the world?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.890
So you started this in,
did you say middle school?

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:26.871
- [Rainn Wilson] Yeah. My
middle school band teacher

00:01:26.871 --> 00:01:31.871
convinced me that it was the
coolest instrument on earth

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.410
and that I'd get all the chicks.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.756
- [Kelly Clarkson] It does look
like a giant bong. (laughs)

00:01:36.756 --> 00:01:37.589
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.589 --> 00:01:38.580
- (chuckles) It really does.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.250
A bassoon bong has not
really been done before.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.886
Well, they're a little pricey,

00:01:42.886 --> 00:01:44.133
so I don't know if that would work.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.650
So I played it all through high school

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.750
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's such
an interesting instrument.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.040
- There's like a parallel world

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.210
in which I didn't become an actor,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.460
I just am like the principal bassoonist

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.130
for like the Indianapolis
Symphony Orchestra.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.283
- I love that life.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.430
Have you ever read "The Midnight Library"?

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.263
- No.

00:02:00.263 --> 00:02:01.096
- [Kelly Clarkson] Okay. It's a good book.

00:02:01.096 --> 00:02:01.929
- And it's like you're in between.

00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:03.595
- Would you read it to me?
- Right now.

00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:06.090
No, but the synopsis is what
your life would look like

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.230
if you took different paths.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.087
- That's like Gwyneth
Paltrow in "Sliding Doors".

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:10.770
- [Kelly Clarkson] It's
a little like that.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.159
Yeah. It's a little,

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:13.170
but it's a quick read.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.003
It's cool.

00:02:14.003 --> 00:02:14.836
- Okay.

00:02:14.836 --> 00:02:16.410
- [Kelly Clarkson] But do
people still recognize you

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.243
from the voice over?

00:02:17.243 --> 00:02:19.530
I mean, I feel like
you're Dwight everywhere.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.640
I feel like you can't go anywhere

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.480
and people still recognize you.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.030
- I will be Dwight to my grave.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.920
- I will be the girl that
sings "Since U Been Gone".

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.843
So, here we go. (chuckles)

00:02:26.843 --> 00:02:27.676
- [Rainn Wilson] You sang that?

00:02:27.676 --> 00:02:28.509
(Kelly and Rainn high fives each other)

00:02:28.509 --> 00:02:29.342
- Yeah. (chuckles)

00:02:29.342 --> 00:02:30.175
- I love that song.

00:02:30.175 --> 00:02:31.500
- That's what I will be.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.350
- Well you're also "Kelly Clarkson!"

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.520
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes. That too.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.540
Thank you, Steve Carell.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.313
Yes, yes. There's that as well.

00:02:39.244 --> 00:02:40.350
- Yeah. What was the question?

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.029
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's all
I've done in my whole career.

00:02:42.029 --> 00:02:43.260
(chuckles) That's what I would say.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.140
No. I heard that you tweeted this.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.150
So let me show everybody what you...

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.950
So you were "At dentist's office.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:50.783
Put on a mask

00:02:50.783 --> 00:02:54.022
because the woman next to me
has a Dunder Mifflin shirt on."

00:02:54.022 --> 00:02:54.855
(audience laughs)

00:02:54.855 --> 00:02:55.688
- Yeah

00:02:55.688 --> 00:02:56.521
- Which you have to be a hardcore fan.

00:02:56.521 --> 00:02:57.750
I'm just saying

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.700
to be wearing that shirt.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.560
One, did your root canal go well?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.640
'Cause you were at the dentist

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.660
and I heard it was a root canal.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.360
But two, do you get
nervous in that situation?

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.193
'Cause you're trapped.

00:03:07.193 --> 00:03:08.026
You're like trapped there.

00:03:08.026 --> 00:03:10.620
So you can't be like
nice and then head off.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.120
- I was going in without a mask

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.590
and I saw her and her kid

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.090
and she had a Dunder Mifflin t-shirt

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.270
and so I was like, "Oh this is so awkward.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.670
I'm gonna have to sit for
15 minutes with this woman."

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.990
So I went and got a mask so-

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.534
- [Kelly Clarkson] Or maybe
longer in the waiting room.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:24.367
- Maybe longer.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.500
So I went in incognito,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.720
so we just didn't have to
have the awkward conversation

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.020
but I appreciate the fans so much.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.730
- But it's not about the
awkward conversation.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.200
It's like, it's a fine conversation

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.940
then it's awkward when it's just quiet

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:36.887
and you've talked about it-

00:03:36.887 --> 00:03:37.720
- Right.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.790
- and you're just sitting
so closely together.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.530
Yeah. That's the awkward part

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.630
where you're like, "Yeah
we're just both here."

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.463
- Post conversation.

00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:44.296
- Yes.

00:03:44.296 --> 00:03:46.290
- But speaking of the root
canal, it's pretty sad.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.317
The doctor was like,

00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:48.840
"Yeah. You know, when you get older

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.949
and you hit middle age,

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:53.010
your nerves and your teeth start to decay

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.010
and rot away and bacteria builds.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.680
I'm like, "Oh my God, I'm decaying!"

00:03:58.680 --> 00:03:59.850
- Debbie Downer.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.240
- That long, slow, inevitable
decay of the human body,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.160
I'm witnessing in front of my dentist.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.120
It was horrible.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.080
- You have like Eeyore for a dentist.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.280
That is some devastating.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.113
- [Rainn Wilson] Yeah.

00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:10.890
- Like why even tell people that?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:11.790
- He's horrible.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.897
Yeah. He's the worst.

00:04:12.897 --> 00:04:14.130
- [Kelly Clarkson] But you know what

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.750
the good thing about a root canal is?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.700
Is that they give you the nitrous.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:18.780
They give you the laughing gas?

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.950
- I'm scared of that.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:20.783
- [Kelly Clarkson] Are you?

00:04:20.783 --> 00:04:21.729
- Yeah. I'm scared like-

00:04:21.729 --> 00:04:22.562
- What does it say about me,

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.910
that I'm like "You
should probably go ahead

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:24.743
and give me more.

00:04:24.743 --> 00:04:26.310
It doesn't affect me as well."

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.530
So I like think it's so fun.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.090
- [Rainn Wilson] I'm afraid
I'm just gonna start talking

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.070
and spill like family secrets.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.665
- [Kelly Clarkson] I don't
care. I spill that already.

00:04:33.665 --> 00:04:34.740
(Rainn Wilson laughs)

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:35.573
Like I don't care.

00:04:35.573 --> 00:04:37.350
I'm like, "I just think it's
the funniest thing ever."

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.232
I always think it feels good. (laughs)

00:04:39.232 --> 00:04:40.082
(Rainn Wilson laughs)

00:04:40.082 --> 00:04:40.915
(audience cheers)

00:04:40.915 --> 00:04:42.007
His new Paramount Plus movie is called

00:04:42.007 --> 00:04:43.641
"Jerry and Marge Go Large".

00:04:43.641 --> 00:04:44.474
(audience continues cheering)

00:04:44.474 --> 00:04:47.640
So this new movie is based
on a true story, right?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.340
- Yeah. It's this real
life couple in Michigan.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.370
And this guy was a math genius, engineer.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.890
And he figured out that
this certain lottery game,

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:59.550
if you played it in the right
way to the right numbers,

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.430
you could actually win in the long haul.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.420
It was kind of-

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.560
- See, I don't call that cheating.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.393
That's just smart.

00:05:05.393 --> 00:05:06.226
- [Rainn Wilson] No, it's not cheating.

00:05:06.226 --> 00:05:07.059
- Yeah.

00:05:07.059 --> 00:05:10.140
- He just saw the math of
this certain lottery game.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:13.800
So he pulled the money of
his town and his family

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.260
and they would drive to Massachusetts

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.820
where the lottery was every week

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.180
and buy like tons of lottery tickets.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.013
- Yeah.

00:05:22.013 --> 00:05:23.790
- And they ended up winning
millions and millions of dollars

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.920
for themselves and for their community,

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.230
more importantly, for the town.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.510
That they put into the town.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.343
- I love that.

00:05:31.343 --> 00:05:32.723
(audience claps)

00:05:32.723 --> 00:05:34.920
And I just think it's crazy

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.570
when people are so "I'm horrible at math,"

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:37.920
but even when people get upset

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.630
and they're like, "Oh they're
counting cards in Vegas."

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.550
I'm like, "If they're
smart enough to do that,

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:42.630
they deserve to win."

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.463
- Absolutely!

00:05:43.463 --> 00:05:45.570
- Yes! If you're smart
enough to get away with it.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.070
That's that's our problem.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:47.903
- No question.

00:05:47.903 --> 00:05:48.788
- [Kelly Clarkson] Not theirs.

00:05:48.788 --> 00:05:49.621
(audience chatters)

00:05:49.621 --> 00:05:51.180
So you described your (chuckles)

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.970
You described your character
as everyone's drunk uncle?

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:54.803
- Yeah.

00:05:54.803 --> 00:05:57.287
- So is this like Cousin Eddie? (chuckles)

00:05:57.287 --> 00:05:59.150
- What was your inspiration?

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.810
- My character Bill in
"Jerry and Marge" is...

00:06:03.698 --> 00:06:06.436
He's like everyone's drunk uncle.

00:06:06.436 --> 00:06:08.087
(Kelly Clarkson laughs hysterically)

00:06:08.087 --> 00:06:08.920
- The vice.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:11.769
- [Rainn Wilson] You know this
guy as soon as you see him.

00:06:11.769 --> 00:06:13.590
He's the one who sells
him the lottery tickets

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.480
from his own liquor store.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.770
It was super fun.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.440
It was kind of the first
big comedy role I've done

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.367
since "The Office".

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:22.108
Yeah. It was a super lot of fun.

00:06:22.108 --> 00:06:22.941
- Cool cast as well.

00:06:22.941 --> 00:06:24.360
- Yeah. Bryan Cranston, he's the best.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.932
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah, Annette Bening.

00:06:25.932 --> 00:06:26.765
- Annette Bening, come on.

00:06:26.765 --> 00:06:27.600
- [Kelly Clarkson] Very, very cool cast.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.520
So what were your uncles
like in real life?

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.230
Did you pull from inspiration?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.200
- Yeah. I have a very interesting family.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.160
- I think we all do, right?

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:35.993
- [Rainn Wilson] Don't we?

00:06:35.993 --> 00:06:36.826
- Yeah, if you're fine.

00:06:36.826 --> 00:06:39.780
- And one of my uncles who
is a dear close friend,

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:43.800
he's a professor of educational
psychology in Idaho.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.633
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh!

00:06:44.633 --> 00:06:46.290
And he studies beauty.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.730
That's him! That's his whole thing.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:49.020
He studies beauty and the effect-

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:49.920
- How we receive it?

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.130
Yeah. The effective beauty
on your consciousness.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.010
Like how uplifting it is
and what it does for you.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.530
And when you recognize beautiful flowers

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:02.730
or beautiful works of art
and it's a fascinating field.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.563
- [Kelly Clarkson] I wonder

00:07:03.563 --> 00:07:04.560
does he ever do the juxtaposition?

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.333
Does he ever, like what it does to us?

00:07:06.333 --> 00:07:09.090
If you walk in somewhere
and it's like a darker vibe

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.620
or it's more depressing, does he?

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.023
- Yeah. Like ugliness or something?

00:07:12.023 --> 00:07:16.620
- Well, I just mean you're
not in a Stepford housewife,

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.090
you're in like the Addams Family's house.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:19.350
Like what does that do to your psyche?

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:20.183
I'm just saying.

00:07:20.183 --> 00:07:21.990
- Well, it certainly is clear

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:25.170
that beauty is incredibly
uplifting and important.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.003
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah. I like that.

00:07:26.003 --> 00:07:27.540
- He's really convinced
that it's the answer.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.280
All the problems in
the world can be solved

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.650
if we put our focus on beauty.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.750
- You also have a travel show,
which I think is awesome.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.430
So you search for happiness.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.860
So, you kind of pull from
your uncle a little bit.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:38.693
- Yeah.

00:07:38.693 --> 00:07:40.680
- Do you think beauty is part of that?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.450
- It's interesting that
we're talking about this

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:43.590
'cause I hadn't really thought about that.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.030
I'm about to leave next week.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:48.060
I go around the world for a show

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.406
called "The Geography Of Bliss",

00:07:50.406 --> 00:07:52.440
looking for happiness around the world

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.970
and what makes people happy?

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:57.090
Why are some cultures so much
better at creating happiness

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.070
in their population than others?

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.200
And what secrets can we find

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.760
and kind of bring back home?

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.920
So going to Bulgaria, and Iceland,

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.040
and Ghana, and Africa,
and Japan, and Thailand.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.840
- Well. Who were you doing this with?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.280
- Peacock Universal.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.540
- Are you traveling with anyone though?

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.550
Like anybody in your
family going or just you?

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.953
- It's just me searching for happiness.

00:08:16.953 --> 00:08:17.786
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's awesome.

00:08:17.786 --> 00:08:19.260
- But I think that this beauty idea

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.240
is something that I should investigate.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.550
- Yeah. I love the idea of
searching for happiness.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.550
They always do that with
what tribes live the longest

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.050
or what areas of the world.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.220
They're called blue something or blue.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.450
I can't remember what they're called.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.283
- Blue zones or something like that.

00:08:31.283 --> 00:08:32.160
- Yeah. Blue zones!

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.210
That's interesting though.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.670
I wonder at the end of your journey,

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.590
if it'll be like, if simple is better

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.970
'cause I feel like we complicate life

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.483
with all the things, right?

00:08:40.483 --> 00:08:42.870
I wonder if people that
you find are living

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.820
more simpler or more happier.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:46.140
- I'm not sure what we'll find.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.550
I mean, there's some-

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:48.540
- [Kelly Clarkson] Iceland's beautiful.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:49.710
- Yes. I've been before.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:50.670
It's incredible.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.780
It's one of my favorite places.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.223
- It's got like so many
things going on there.

00:08:53.223 --> 00:08:54.540
Like the black thing, the waterfall,

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.500
there's like so many things.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.530
- Yeah. I've been already
four times to Iceland

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.873
and it's one of the
happiest places on Earth.

00:09:02.207 --> 00:09:04.406
And it's incredible
because just like you said,

00:09:04.406 --> 00:09:06.420
you'll be sitting on a black sand beach,

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.340
there's a glacier on one side of you,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.010
there's hot springs over here.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.410
There's like a thousand
foot waterfall behind you.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.577
And then you've seen like
10 of those and you're like,

00:09:15.577 --> 00:09:18.866
"Ho hum. Oh geez, another
thousand foot waterfall."

00:09:18.866 --> 00:09:20.700
- [Kelly Clarkson] I think
that affects us too though.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.590
Happiness. That's why I
like to get outta the city

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:23.423
and go into nature.

00:09:23.423 --> 00:09:24.360
I think nature.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.130
That's obviously why you
have a place in Oregon,

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.197
like the cabin just to get out.

00:09:27.197 --> 00:09:28.514
- Yeah. It's good to get out of the city.

00:09:28.514 --> 00:09:29.347
- Yeah, it feels good.

00:09:29.347 --> 00:09:30.180
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.013
- [Kelly Clarkson] All right.

00:09:31.013 --> 00:09:32.190
- We need another break.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.890
Stream Rainn's movie,
"Jerry and Marge Go Large"

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:38.160
on Paramount Plus and look for
him soon traveling the world

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.370
in "Rainn Wilson &amp; The
Geography Of Bliss" on Peacock,

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.480
which I will not be missing.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.630
I'm excited about that.

